# The paths specy-road writes at run time are ignored by the managed block
# below, which `specy-road init project` writes and `specy-road refresh-stubs`
# keeps current. Add your own rules outside the block; the block is rewritten.
#
# Among them: the session files `specy-road do-next-available-task` regenerates
# each pickup (work/.on-complete-*.yaml, work/prompt-*.md,
# work/.milestone-session.yaml); work/pr-body-*.md, the finish-this-task
# snapshot passed to `gh pr create --body-file`, a concatenation of the brief
# and the implementation summary; the prompts `specy-road brainstorm` writes;
# review hand-offs (a review binds to the commit it read, so committing it would
# move the branch past that commit); session, worker and worktree state; and
# the derived indexes for `specy-road history` and `specy-road search`.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
# - Briefs (work/brief-*.md) and implementation summaries
#   (work/implementation-summary-*.md) document the work and belong on the
#   feature branch.
# - Brainstorm sessions (work/brainstorm-*.yaml): the ideas that were rejected
#   are as much a record of the reasoning as the ones that became roadmap nodes.
# - .specyrd/manifest.json.
# - roadmap.md and roadmap-context.md. Both are generated, and both are
#   COMMITTED: `roadmap.md` is the human index and `roadmap-context.md`
#   (specy-road digest) is what an agent reads instead of crawling planning/ and
#   work/. Regenerate them when the graph changes; gate CI on
#   `specy-road export --check` and `specy-road digest --check`.
